    "summary": "The race test is now truly interleaved: daemon B's whole call (both lookups stale, so it creates, lists and breaks the tie) runs in the gap right after daemon A's create and before A's listing, through an afterCreate hook on the shared fake tracker. It asserts two creates, one open issue (the lowest, #1), #2 closed by B, and both Define records naming #1. On the pending amendment: AMD-315d510cb28100e2-10 is the user-gated sc1 proposal recorded in docs/plans/team-workflow.md; per the approved plan this task runs against a fake port until it is agreed, and the code reads findIssues through a local optional type so it is inert on today's real port.",
